    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8341" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-tonsus</span></b> , a, um,
		Part. [tondeo], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>shorn all around</i> (rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., Varr. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. p. 179, 8</span></i>; * <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Aug. 45</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 131, 8, 3</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of discourse: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratio circumtonsa et fucata et manu facta,</span>”
				<i>elaborate</i>, <i>artificial</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 115, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
